WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.369 --> 00:00:06.369
This is a simulated room with eight Wi-Fi sensors on the walls.

2
00:00:06.371 --> 00:00:13.371
The white figure is a simulated person. ECHOSPACE never sees it, only the radio signals it disturbs.

3
00:00:13.687 --> 00:00:21.687
The violet ring is where the system thinks the person is, worked out from those signals alone.

4
00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:29.689
The green points are the parts of the room it believes are occupied.

5
00:00:29.691 --> 00:00:39.691
As the person walks, the detection follows. The status line shows how far off it is.

6
00:00:44.565 --> 00:00:53.565
Sitting still is harder. A still body disturbs the signal much less than a moving one.

7
00:00:53.566 --> 00:01:02.566
The system keeps the person once found, but the estimate drifts more.

8
00:01:06.694 --> 00:01:15.694
Here the person walks behind a partition wall. Radio passes through it, weakened.

9
00:01:15.695 --> 00:01:24.695
The detection still follows, with more error near the wall.

10
00:01:27.697 --> 00:01:34.697
Everything here is simulated. Real hardware would need its own testing.
